---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { lastmodForPath } from '../lib/lastmod.mjs';

const updated = lastmodForPath(Astro.url.pathname);
---
<Base
  title="Privacy: what Taxfold and taxfold.app collect"
  description="The Taxfold app collects no data; your receipts stay on your iPhone. This website runs cookieless Cloudflare Web Analytics. Here is each part."
>
  <article class="prose">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight mb-6">Privacy</h1>

    <p>
      This page covers two things: the Taxfold iPhone app, and this website, taxfold.app. They are different, so we
      describe them separately. Both are run by Opal Harmony P.C., the company that makes Taxfold.
    </p>

    <h2>The app: we collect nothing</h2>
    <p>
      The Taxfold app sends us no data. There is no account, no sign-in, no sync server, no bank connection and no
      analytics or advertising code in the app. The receipts you scan, their photos and everything you type stay in
      the app's storage on your iPhone. When the app is listed, its App Store privacy label will read
      <strong>"Data Not Collected"</strong>.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Reading receipts</strong> happens on the iPhone, with Apple's built-in text recognition. The images
        are not uploaded anywhere.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Camera and Photos</strong> are used only when you scan or import a receipt, and only with your
        permission.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Exports</strong> (CSV or PDF) go only where you send them with the iPhone share sheet.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Backups:</strong> if you back up your iPhone with iCloud Backup or to a computer, the app's data is
        part of that backup, held by Apple or on your computer under your control. We have no access to it.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Purchases</strong> go through Apple. Apple tells us aggregate sales figures, not who you are.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Because nothing reaches us, deleting the app deletes your Taxfold data from the phone. Export what you want to
      keep first.
    </p>

    <h2>This website: cookieless analytics</h2>
    <p>
      "We collect nothing" would not be true of the website, so here is what it does. taxfold.app is hosted on
      Cloudflare and runs <strong>Cloudflare Web Analytics</strong> to count visits.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>No cookies, no fingerprinting.</strong> In Cloudflare's words, Web Analytics "does not use any
        client-side state, such as cookies or localStorage, to collect usage metrics", and Cloudflare does not
        "fingerprint" individuals via their IP address, User Agent string, or any other data.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>What it records:</strong> page views and visits, the referring site, and page-load timing, which we
        see only as aggregate counts. A small script from <code>static.cloudflareinsights.com</code> loads on each
        page to report them.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Delivering pages:</strong> like any web host, Cloudflare processes your IP address and browser
        details to serve the site and protect it from abuse.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Search statistics:</strong> Google Search Console shows us which searches led to the site, as
        aggregate numbers from Google. It puts nothing on this site.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      The site has no sign-up form, no ads and no other trackers.
    </p>

    <h2>Email</h2>
    <p>
      If you write to us, we receive your email address and your message, and use them only to reply. Mail to
      taxfold.app addresses is forwarded through Cloudflare Email Routing to the inbox we read.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights and contact</h2>
    <p>
      Under the GDPR you can ask what we hold about you, and ask us to correct or delete it. For the app there is
      nothing to ask for: the data is on your phone. For email, write to
      <a href="mailto:privacy@taxfold.app">privacy@taxfold.app</a>. You can also complain to your data protection
      authority; in Greece that is the Hellenic Data Protection Authority.
    </p>
    <p class="text-sm text-ink-soft">
      Last updated <time datetime={updated.toISOString()}>{updated.toISOString().slice(0, 10)}</time>.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
